═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ what-ran ← §§ experiment-design                                      ⊞
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  scale-up :
    Session-14 base : Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct
    Session-16 base : Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct  (3× params)

  isolation :
    joint     — v1.3.0-baseline recipe ; EN-prompt → CSL-completion
                (prompt-masked from loss)
    csl-only  — pure LM loss on CSL content only
    en-only   — pure LM loss on EN paraphrase only

  training config (all three) :
    rank = 16 , epochs = 3 , lr = 2e-4 cosine , max-len = 1024
    LoRA targets = [q, k, v, o]_proj
    dtype = bf16-if-cuda else fp32 ; actual = fp32 on this CPU
    wallclock ≈ 7.3 min per adapter on 10-core CPU

  measurement :
    pre-tune  : Qwen2.5-1.5B base alone vs 10 fixtures
    post-tune : base + adapter attached vs same 10 fixtures
    metric    : mean token-NLL under causal-LM teacher-forcing

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ results ← §§ H1-H2 verdicts                                           ∫
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  pre-tune mean m₂ (Qwen2.5-1.5B base alone) : 1.0958

  | adapter   | post m₂ | Δ m₂    | Δ CSL-NLL | Δ EN-NLL | signature     | H1 | H2 |
  |-----------|--------:|--------:|----------:|---------:|---------------|:--:|:--:|
  | joint     |  1.1111 | +0.0153 |    -0.069 |   -0.097 | balanced-EN   | ✗ | ✗ |
  | csl-only  |  1.0468 | -0.0490 |    -0.170 |   -0.042 | CSL-dominant  | ✓ | ✓ |
  | en-only   |  1.1317 | +0.0359 |    -0.043 |   -0.119 | EN-dominant   | ✗ | ✗ |

  interpretation :
    csl-only lowered CSL-NLL by 4× the amount it lowered EN-NLL → the
      adapter is genuinely learning the CSL token-distribution as a
      distinct phenomenon, not as a regularization side-effect.
    en-only lowered EN-NLL by 3× the amount it lowered CSL-NLL → the
      symmetric confirmation ; the pipeline isn't accidentally biased
      toward CSL ; each training target drives its matching
      distribution harder.
    joint behaved like a mild EN-dominant run, probably because the
      prompt half (EN) influences the base representation even though
      its tokens are masked from the backward pass.

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ why this matters ← §§ density-claim-substance                       I>
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The m₂ metric (NLL-ratio CSL/EN) is a proxy for "notation density
  relative to English in the eyes of a trained LLM." Before this
  session there was a reasonable critique : maybe the metric only
  reflects model-inherent bias against out-of-distribution tokens,
  and any fine-tune would lower it regardless. Session-14's negative
  result did not rule this out.

  Session-16's isolation experiment rules it out :
    - CSL-only training moves m₂ TOWARD 1.0 (-0.049).
    - EN-only training moves m₂ AWAY from 1.0 (+0.036).
    - Joint training (mixed) barely moves m₂ in either direction.

  The 3-way split is the signature of a metric that is SPECIFIC to
  the distribution being trained, not a regularization artifact.
  This is the first such demonstration on the CSLv3 corpus.

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ caveats ← §§ honest-science                                         ◐
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  ◐ Training on the same corpus as measurement (data leakage).
    Generalization-test on a held-out fixture set is Session-17+ work.
    The current result only shows the ADAPTER CAN learn on this
    corpus ; it does NOT show m₂ moves on unseen CSL.
  ◐ 3 epochs × 10 pairs × LoRA rank 16 is small. Larger scale
    (longer training, larger corpus, larger base, CUDA) expected to
    amplify the signal.
  ◐ CPU-only. Intel Arc A770 has Vulkan but no CUDA torch. ROCm-via-
    DirectML or IPEX would be Session-17+ infrastructure items.
  ◐ Rank sweep {4, 16, 32, 64} not performed ; rank=16 chosen from
    published LoRA priors. Sensitivity analysis is Session-17 scope.

